James sought assistance with setting up a CodeOcean repository using R and the `sf` package, which required manual installation of the `s2` package. He provided his Docker file and main R script, including error messages encountered during the build process, particularly related to missing `absl_base` during the `s2` installation. I diagnosed the issue as primarily linked to the `PKG_CONFIG_PATH`, advising him to avoid manually installing `s2` and instead install `sf` with its dependencies. I recommended updates to the Docker setup, such as including the `build-essential` package and avoiding version pinning. I also provided troubleshooting steps, such as unsetting `PKG_CONFIG_PATH` and using verbose mode for installations. The best guess for resolution involved removing the manual installation of `s2`, unsetting `PKG_CONFIG_PATH`, and directly installing `sf`.
